  "summary": "Kalakshetra was founded on 6 January 1936 by Rukmini Devi Arundale within the Theosophical Society in Adyar and moved to its 100-acre seaside campus at Thiruvanmiyur in 1962. It became an Institute of National Importance by an Act of Parliament in 1993 and is an autonomous body under the Ministry of Culture. Its Rukmini Devi College of Fine Arts runs four-year diploma courses in Bharatanatyam, Carnatic music and visual arts, admitted through a practical aptitude test and interview.",
